---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { page } from '../lib/asset';
---

<Layout
  title="Refund Policy — codescribe"
  description="14-day refund policy for codescribe purchases, including EU consumer distance-selling rights."
  path="refunds"
>
  <LegalPage title="Refund Policy" eyebrow="Trust · Refunds">
    <p class="note">
      [?] Draft aligned with common Merchant of Record (MoR) and EU distance-selling
      practice. Final wording must match the MoR checkout terms you sign with
      (for example Paddle / Lemon Squeezy / Stripe). If MoR terms and this page
      differ, the MoR checkout terms control for that purchase.
    </p>

    <h2>14-day no-questions refund (consumers)</h2>
    <p>
      If you buy a personal codescribe license as a consumer and you are not
      satisfied, you may request a full refund within <strong>14 days</strong>
      of purchase. For EU/EEA/UK consumers buying online (distance selling),
      this aligns with the statutory cooling-off period where it applies.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>No product review quiz is required for a timely first refund request.</li>
      <li>Request by emailing
        <a href="mailto:hello@vetcoders.io?subject=codescribe%20refund">hello@vetcoders.io</a>
        with your order email and order ID / receipt from checkout.
      </li>
      <li>We aim to confirm and process refunds within <strong>2 business days</strong>
        of a complete request; card settlement may take longer depending on your bank.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How to request</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Email <a href="mailto:hello@vetcoders.io">hello@vetcoders.io</a> with subject line “codescribe refund”.</li>
      <li>Include the email used at checkout and the order or invoice ID.</li>
      <li>If the MoR portal offers a self-serve cancel/refund, you may use that instead — same 14-day window.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Business / VAT invoices</h2>
    <p>
      Purchases invoiced to a business (B2B) may follow the MoR’s business
      refund rules rather than the consumer cooling-off period. Contact us and
      we will apply the correct path for your receipt type.
    </p>

    <h2>After 14 days</h2>
    <p>
      Outside the 14-day window we may still offer goodwill refunds for
      clear technical failure (for example the app cannot launch on a supported
      Apple Silicon Mac after reasonable troubleshooting). Those are case-by-case,
      not guaranteed.
    </p>

    <h2>Chargebacks</h2>
    <p>
      Please contact us before filing a chargeback so we can reverse the charge
      cleanly. Chargebacks opened while a refund is already in progress can
      delay resolution.
    </p>

    <h2>Related</h2>
    <p>
      <a href={page('terms')}>Terms of Use &amp; EULA</a>
      · <a href={page('support')}>Support</a>
      · <a href={page('privacy')}>Privacy Policy</a>
    </p>
  </LegalPage>
</Layout>
